# TK3: # TIMED ARM A (the control) of the paired ABAB for lever 'stack' on coding prompts, EIGHT users live, audits OFF. A = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate (the control: the nine levers, two quad blocks,
# the in-trace sampler, 262k windows), B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate-stack (the control MINUS QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE plus QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX=1, QWEN_FAST_TP4_DRAFT_CONV=1 and QWEN_FAST_TP4_DRAFT_HEADS=1). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order.
# The tests: warmup, one coding stream, concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix: it is here so the smoke check can judge both blocks, two quad markers and a both-quads round), eight
# 32k code users and eight about 120,000-token code users (800 out), eight live at once.
# READ: [PACKED-PHASE] rounds at live=8, PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians (check the load average around the run: a busy host skews a timed phase 10-20%, so no build,
# no CI push and no other job beside it); the per-seat rate = committed tokens per round per user / round time; the SMOKE_JSON hashes equal between the arms (a lever that is exact or
# tau-only never changes the served text). Offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 --position-keyed
# --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0: every verified proposal identical (the three levers are exact)).
# The STACK: nosamp + S1 + D2 together, the three exact round levers, no tau lever. Estimate about -20 ms of an eight-live round. READ it against the single-lever pairs of this window:
# the sum of the single deltas is the prediction; a stack gaining less is the finding (a shared cost) and a stall here with all of H1-H3 clean is a lever interaction. Markers: both the
# S1 and the D2 engaged lines, no fall-back line, no in_trace=1 sampler line. Tau report as the D2 pair's.
# The smoke check fails the arm on a fall-back line or on no engaged line for its lever. A stall is a finding. Duration (estimate): 90 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8-x experiments window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8-x and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-x-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8-x commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-x-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k
